unit: REVIEW-audit-daemon-2
commits: c9cff4dd6 (the audit)
what: audited the host-crate range cafc95dd7..HEAD — dm-daemon-api-edge, the
  cli composition move, the daemon parts and REVIEW-build-index-read-port — end
  to end. Row claims verified: no host-tagged module remains in sovereign-mesh
  (0/28) or sovereign-api (0/1); crate-lines --crate sovereign-daemon reads
  78,021 lines / 126 rows (read with the coverage-hole assertion bypassed — the
  instrument refuses on the deferred corpus-index hole); boundary-gate exit=0
  with no new [[exception]]; no shim is deletable here (every sovereign_api::
  path has zero importers, but the shims retire with the crate at
  REVIEW-build-sovereign-api-retire).
  Fixes:
  - ARCH 5 (TESTALL red): CONCEPTS.toml EvidenceSet canonical ->
    corpus_index::index::EvidenceSet (destination.rs's positive-control list
    too); chunk_provenance_census scanned only corpus-engine/src so the two
    acquired_from_* doors read as gone (scan corpus-index/src too);
    f26_egress_census rows for moved files (ring_sync test modules moved to
    tests/main/, out of the production-src scope -> rows removed; three routes
    sovereign-api -> sovereign-daemon -> re-keyed);
    conformance_tags_are_fresh (sovereign-api.toml had no covers: tags left ->
    deleted, six claims land in sovereign-daemon.toml).
  - ARCH 3.2 (arch-gate): baselines/oversized.txt rows re-keyed to
    corpus-index/src/index/{mod,search}.rs (path re-key, counts unchanged).
  - ARCH 3.1 (layout-gate): layout_gate.rs DECIDER ->
    corpus-index/src/corpus.rs.
  - ARCH 3 (doc drift): daemon_cmd/<moved> repointed in 11 live docs/configs
    (including the LIVE mutant target quality/sabotage/all.toml:409) and 14
    .rs doc comments; rustfmt drift in 17 files fixed with cargo fmt --all.
  Recorded, not changed: the corpus-index (19), sovereign-peer-wire (1) and
  understanding-atlas (13) coverage holes (deferred by the 2026-09-18 priority
  cut; sovereign-peer-wire needs a tag row); sovereign/HISTORY.md and the
  handed order keep their historical daemon_cmd spellings; size-gate is the
  advisory warn_gate, not re-pinned.
checks: TESTALL exit=0 (13397 pass, 0 fail); PREPUSH exit=0 (3 of 18 want
  attention: size-gate warn_gate by design, instrument-gate and hook-wiring
  out of budget / could-not-judge).
